hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1450","On the authority of Bishr ibn Muadh Al-Aqdi, on the authority of Bishr ibn Al-Mufaddal, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman ibn Muawiyah, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhubab, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, who said: I never saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, raising his hands, ever calling on his pulpit or anywhere else. But I saw him saying this: and he pointed with his index finger to move it.” Abu Bakr said: Abd al-Rahman bin Muawiyah. This is Abu al-Huwayrith, a Madani."
